fix(cli): innsegl retire presents a credential to the lifecycle listener (#268)

The identity-lifecycle listener has required a repository-scoped credential
since #264, and `serve` refuses to start a split listener without a key set,
so wherever that listener exists the credential is mandatory. #266 surveyed
the callers that existed on its branch and fixed both; `retire` was written
on the other epic and was invisible to that survey. On the merged tree it
presented nothing, and reported the 401 as UNREACHABLE - which sends an
operator to restart a deployment that is up and answering.

The credential authorises a REPOSITORY and this command names a RUN, and only
the listener knows which repository holds a run. That circle is cut outside
the protocol: -repo, then $INNSEGL_REPO_ID, then the working tree's origin,
resolved lazily so a listener that enforces nothing reads no environment and
runs no git. The working tree is last and not the only way, because the run
this command exists for is a stranded one.

A refusal is status 21, not 20. The listener answered; the move is to mint a
credential, not to restart anything, and the message names the mint command.
Nothing is renumbered.

